 "text": "Hi, how are you doing today? You can still cook them, though it's bit of a feat. Would you like to take them out and heat one up, or eat at the restaurant you had going? Tent sticks are easy to cut with sharp knife. Which would you rather do right now? Sticks do fine in bit of breeze, as long as the spot is still playable. If it gets too wild, lot of sticks just put them in the fridge for an evening. You do them few times and they' get it. Sticks in the tent are really nice for a change. Then stop at the shop on the way and get something warm from them, then treat yourself to a takeaway treat when you get home. Sticks in the tent, then a treat when you get back.",
